IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-seat`

-- Cases for the seat layer (euca-seat.l4): the questions of the individual to whom the Federal-State
-- Extended Unemployment Compensation Act of 1970 is applied. At least one case for every question,
-- and the cases that the Act does not decide ("not covered"), each asserted.
-- Every expected value below was worked out by hand from the text of the Act before the file was
-- run; a note beside each case says what the hand calculation was.
--
-- THE PERSON. A worker in a State whose extended benefit period began with the week of 3 February
-- 2013 and is still in effect. Their benefit year ran 1 March 2012 to 28 February 2013. They claim
-- for the week of 3 March 2013. Regular compensation payable in the year was 10,000 and was all
-- paid; the weekly benefit amount is 400.

§ `Cases for the individual's questions`

§§ `Section 202(a)(1) and (2)`

-- The week begins 3 March 2013, after the benefit year ended on 28 February 2013: rights have expired,
-- though the person had not received everything available.
#ASSERT `Have I used up my regular unemployment compensation` (Date 3 3 2013) FALSE (Date 28 2 2013)
-- The week begins 24 February 2013, inside the benefit year, and compensation is still available: not used up.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I used up my regular unemployment compensation` (Date 24 2 2013) FALSE (Date 28 2 2013))
-- Everything available received: used up even inside the benefit year.
#ASSERT `Have I used up my regular unemployment compensation` (Date 24 2 2013) TRUE (Date 28 2 2013)

-- No other rights at all: free.
#ASSERT `Am I free of any other right to compensation for this week` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A right to regular compensation under the State law, another State's law, other Federal law, or Canada's law: not free.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I free of any other right to compensation for this week` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I free of any other right to compensation for this week` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I free of any other right to compensation for this week` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I free of any other right to compensation for this week` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- The State rule is applied unless it is inconsistent with the Act.
#ASSERT `Does my State's rule for regular claims also apply to my extended claim` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my State's rule for regular claims also apply to my extended claim` TRUE)

§§ `Section 202(a)(3): the work test`

-- Offered work within my capabilities, no showing of good prospects, 500 a week against a benefit of 400, no supplemental
-- benefits, in writing, State law would deny, 10 an hour against federal 7.25 and no State minimum: turning it down is a denial.
#ASSERT `Will I be denied extended compensation if I turn down this job` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 400 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 7.25 0
-- The same job at exactly 400 a week: not above the benefit amount, so subparagraph D(i) lets me turn it down.
#ASSERT NOT (`Will I be denied extended compensation if I turn down this job` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 400 400 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 7.25 0)
-- The same job paying 7 an hour, below the federal minimum 7.25: D(iv).
#ASSERT NOT (`Will I be denied extended compensation if I turn down this job` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 400 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 7 7.25 0)
-- A referral to a job outside my capabilities: not suitable work, so no denial.
#ASSERT NOT (`Will I be denied extended compensation if I turn down this job` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500 400 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 7.25 0)

#ASSERT `Is this job suitable work for me` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Good prospects shown: the State law decides, and it says no.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this job suitable work for me` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is this job suitable work for me` FALSE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `Am I treated as actively seeking work this week` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I treated as actively seeking work this week` TRUE FALSE)

-- Not seeking work, no excuse: denied.
#ASSERT `Will I be denied extended compensation this week for not seeking work` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- On jury duty under a summons, the State excuses it for regular benefits and has chosen to for extended: not denied.
#ASSERT NOT (`Will I be denied extended compensation this week for not seeking work` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The State has not chosen to extend the jury excuse to extended benefits: denied.
#ASSERT `Will I be denied extended compensation this week for not seeking work` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Seeking work properly: not denied.
#ASSERT NOT (`Will I be denied extended compensation this week for not seeking work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- An earlier failure in the week of 3 February 2013; claiming for the week of 17 March 2013; 3 weeks of work and 1,000 earned, benefit 400:
-- 4 weeks and 1,600 are needed: still ineligible.
#ASSERT `Am I still ineligible this week because of an earlier failure` (Date 17 3 2013) TRUE (Date 3 2 2013) 3 1000 400
-- 4 weeks and 1,600 earned: the ineligibility has ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I still ineligible this week because of an earlier failure` (Date 17 3 2013) TRUE (Date 3 2 2013) 4 1600 400)
-- No failure: never ineligible.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I still ineligible this week because of an earlier failure` (Date 17 3 2013) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) 0 0 400)
-- 3 weeks worked: 1 more. 5 weeks worked: none.
#ASSERT `How many more weeks of work do I need to end my ineligibility` 3 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `How many more weeks of work do I need to end my ineligibility` 5 EQUALS 0
-- 4 x 400 = 1,600, less 1,000 earned: 600 more. 2,000 earned: none.
#ASSERT `How much more must I earn to end my ineligibility` 1000 400 EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `How much more must I earn to end my ineligibility` 2000 400 EQUALS 0

§§ `Section 202(a)(4), (5), (7)`

-- Disqualified for leaving voluntarily; the State law ended it, but not on the strength of later work: still bars.
#ASSERT `Does an earlier disqualification still bar my extended compensation this week` (Date 17 3 2013) `voluntarily leaving employment` TRUE FALSE
-- Ended on the strength of later employment: does not bar.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does an earlier disqualification still bar my extended compensation this week` (Date 17 3 2013) `voluntarily leaving employment` TRUE TRUE)
-- Not ended, but the week is in the period when paragraph (4) does not apply (after 6 March 1993, before 1 January 1995): not barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does an earlier disqualification still bar my extended compensation this week` (Date 1 6 1993) `refusing suitable employment` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does an earlier disqualification still bar my extended compensation this week` (Date 1 6 1995) `refusing suitable employment` FALSE FALSE

-- The State uses the 20-weeks method only: 52 weeks has it; 19 lacks it.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough employment in my base period to get extended compensation` 52 20000 300 6000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the individual has the required employment`
#ASSERT `Do I have enough employment in my base period to get extended compensation` 19 99999 300 6000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the individual lacks the required employment`
-- Earnings must EXCEED 40 times 300 = 12,000.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough employment in my base period to get extended compensation` 0 12000 300 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the individual lacks the required employment`
#ASSERT `Do I have enough employment in my base period to get extended compensation` 0 12001 300 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the individual has the required employment`
-- NOT COVERED: the State law has chosen no method; the Act requires it to, so the Act itself does not say.
#ASSERT `Do I have enough employment in my base period to get extended compensation` 52 99999 300 6000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the State law has chosen no method, which section 202(a)(5) requires it to do`

#ASSERT `Is the work test in force for this week` (Date 3 3 2013)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the work test in force for this week` (Date 1 6 1993))
#ASSERT `Is the work test in force for this week` (Date 6 3 1993)
#ASSERT `Is the work test in force for this week` (Date 1 1 1995)

§§ `Section 202(b): the account`

-- Total payable 10,000, benefit 400, paid 10,000: (A) 5,000; (B) 5,200; (C) 15,600 - 10,000 = 5,600: the least, 5,000.
#ASSERT `How much extended compensation must my account hold` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 5000
-- In a high unemployment period: (A) 8,000; (B) 8,000; (C) 18,400 - 10,000 = 8,400: 8,000.
#ASSERT `How much extended compensation must my account hold` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS 8000
-- The State reduces by 700 of additional compensation: 4,300.
#ASSERT `How much extended compensation must my account hold` 10000 400 10000 TRUE 700 FALSE EQUALS 4300

-- 5,000 at 400 a week is 12.5, so 12 whole weeks; in a high unemployment period 8,000 at 400 is 20.
#ASSERT `For how many whole weeks will my extended compensation account pay` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE 400 EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `For how many whole weeks will my extended compensation account pay` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 TRUE 400 EQUALS JUST 20
-- NOT COVERED: a weekly amount of 0 cannot be divided into; the answer is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `For how many whole weeks will my extended compensation account pay` 10000 400 10000 FALSE 0 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- The 8 per cent test was first met in the week of 13 January 2013: the period begins in the third week after, 3 February 2013, and has no end yet.
#ASSERT `Is the week I am claiming for in a high unemployment period` (Date 3 3 2013) TRUE (Date 13 1 2013) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900)
-- The week of 27 January 2013 is before it began.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the week I am claiming for in a high unemployment period` (Date 27 1 2013) TRUE (Date 13 1 2013) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900))
-- It stopped being met in the week of 10 February 2013: the period runs at least 13 weeks, to 28 April 2013; 21 April is in, 5 May is out.
#ASSERT `Is the week I am claiming for in a high unemployment period` (Date 21 4 2013) TRUE (Date 13 1 2013) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE (Date 10 2 2013)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the week I am claiming for in a high unemployment period` (Date 5 5 2013) TRUE (Date 13 1 2013) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) TRUE (Date 10 2 2013))
-- The 8 per cent test was never met: no high unemployment period.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the week I am claiming for in a high unemployment period` (Date 3 3 2013) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900))

§§ `Section 202(c): interstate claims`

-- Third week on the claim (2 earlier), no period in the State where I filed: cut off.
#ASSERT `Is extended compensation on my interstate claim cut off for this week` TRUE FALSE 2
-- Second week (1 earlier): the first 2 weeks are exempt.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is extended compensation on my interstate claim cut off for this week` TRUE FALSE 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is extended compensation on my interstate claim cut off for this week` TRUE TRUE 5)

§§ `Section 202(a), (b), (c) together`

-- The whole of section 202 for one week; the facts that do not change between the cases are fixed here.
-- The week begins 3 March 2013: benefit year 1 March 2012 to 28 February 2013, period from 3 February 2013 still in effect,
-- all regular compensation not yet received (the year has simply expired), no other rights, no job offer, seeking work, no earlier
-- failure, no disqualification, 52 weeks of employment under the 20-weeks method, no interstate claim, an account of 5,000.
